1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,121
On September 2, 1945, General Douglas
MacArthur signed Japan's surrender.

2
00:00:06,161 --> 00:00:11,351
Then he turned and handed a pen to
the thin general standing behind him.

3
00:00:11,391 --> 00:00:14,976
Three years earlier,
that man had surrendered to Japan.

4
00:00:15,016 --> 00:00:17,340
His name was Jonathan Wainwright.

5
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:21,260
In March 1942,
MacArthur left the Philippines,

6
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:25,291
and Wainwright took command
of the men left behind.

7
00:00:25,331 --> 00:00:29,371
On the island fortress of Corregidor
they held out under constant shelling

8
00:00:29,411 --> 00:00:31,119
until May 6.

9
00:00:31,159 --> 00:00:34,790
Then he surrendered
to save the lives of his men.

10
00:00:34,830 --> 00:00:37,840
The Japanese took him
to a radio station in Manila

11
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:41,650
and made him read
the surrender orders on air.

12
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:45,598
He became the highest-ranking
American prisoner of the war.

13
00:00:45,638 --> 00:00:50,658
For more than three years he was moved
from camp to camp, as far as Manchuria,

14
00:00:50,698 --> 00:00:56,063
afraid that America would remember him
as the general who gave up.

15
00:00:56,103 --> 00:01:00,300
In August 1945,
Soviet troops freed him.

16
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:03,776
Two weeks later he stood
on the deck of the USS Missouri.

17
00:01:03,816 --> 00:01:06,816
Weeks after that,
he received the Medal of Honor,

18
00:01:06,856 --> 00:01:11,332
the award MacArthur
had blocked in 1942.

19
00:01:11,372 --> 00:01:14,402
The man who had been
forced to surrender

20
00:01:14,442 --> 00:01:17,002
watched Japan do the same.
